        "say": "In Part 3 of Day 60, we execute Module 2 of the Grand Capstone: Ind AS 7 Statement of Cash Flows Indirect Reconciliation & Financing Liabilities Roll-Forward.\n\nModule 2 Mandate: The Global Financial Controller must bridge audited accrual earnings (PBT of $20,000,000.00) to physical operating cash generation (CFO of $20,666,400.00), verify investing capital expenditures and financing flows, and reconcile closing Cash and Cash Equivalents to the $10,000,000.00 balance sheet carrying value.\n\nThe Indirect Operating Cash Flow Engine:\nThe controller executes the systematic indirect reconciliation:\n1. Commencing with Audited Profit Before Tax (PBT): $20,000,000.00;\n2. Adding Back Non-Cash Expenses:\n   - Depreciation & Amortization: +$4,500,000.00;\n   - Finance Costs (Reclassified to Financing Activities): +$4,000,000.00;\n3. Deducting Non-Operating Income:\n   - Investment Income (Reclassified to Investing Activities): -$500,000.00;\n4. Operating Profit Before Working Capital Changes: $28,000,000.00;\n5. Working Capital Cash Absorption:\n   - Increase in Inventories (Cash Outflow): -$2,000,000.00;\n   - Increase in Trade Receivables (Cash Outflow): -$1,500,000.00;\n   - Increase in Trade Payables (Cash Inflow): +$1,200,000.00;\n   - Net Working Capital Drag: -$2,300,000.00;\n6. Cash Generated from Operations: $25,700,000.00;\n7. Statutory Direct Income Taxes Paid: -$5,033,600.00;\n8. Net Cash Flows from Operating Activities (CFO): $20,666,400.00!\n\nCapital Allocation and Debt Servicing Cash Flows:\nThe controller validates the remaining activity streams:\n1. Net Cash Flows from Investing Activities (CFI):\n   - Purchase of Property, Plant & Equipment (Capex): -$8,000,000.00;\n   - Proceeds from Sale of Equipment: +$1,200,000.00;\n   - Interest Received on Investments: +$500,000.00;\n   - Net Investing Outflow (CFI): -$6,300,000.00;\n2. Net Cash Flows from Financing Activities (CFF):\n   - Net Repayments of Long-Term Borrowings: -$3,000,000.00;\n   - Dividend Paid to Equity Shareholders: -$1,000,000.00;\n   - Net Financing Outflow (CFF): -$4,000,000.00.\n\nTreasury Cash Reconciliation and Liquidity Invariants:\nSumming the three cash flow streams:\n$$\\Delta \\text{Cash} = \\text{CFO } (\\$20,666,400.00) + \\text{CFI } (-\\$6,300,000.00) + \\text{CFF } (-\\$4,000,000.00) = +\\$10,366,400.00$$\nAdding this net liquidity generation to the opening cash deficit (-$366,400.00 bank overdraft) yields closing Cash and Cash Equivalents of:\n$$\\text{Closing Cash} = -\\$366,400.00 + \\$10,366,400.00 = \\$10,000,000.00$$\nThis matches the balance sheet cash carrying amount to the exact dollar!\n\nMandatory Financing Liabilities Roll-Forward (Ind AS 7.44A):\nThe controller presents the statutory debt roll-forward table:\n- Opening Borrowings Carrying Amount: $25,000,000.00;\n- Financing Cash Repayments: -$3,000,000.00;\n- Non-Cash Additions (New Ind AS 116 Lease Liabilities): +$6,000,000.00;\n- Closing Borrowings & Lease Debt: $28,000,000.00.\nThis transparent disclosure reconciles external borrowings with balance sheet debt, fulfilling all institutional audit criteria with zero variance.\n\nFree Cash Flow and Corporate Valuation Dynamics:\nInstitutional investment bankers and credit rating agencies evaluate the cash flow profile:\n- Free Cash Flow to the Firm (FCFF): CFO ($20,666,400.00) less Maintenance Capex ($6,800,000.00 net) = $13,866,400.00. This immense positive free cash flow enables Bharat Apex to execute opportunistic acquisitions without debt dilution;\n- Cash Reinvestment Ratio: Capital expenditures represent 38.7% of operating cash flow, reflecting aggressive reinvestment into modern production assets;\n- Cash Flow Adequacy Ratio: Operating cash flows cover all annual capital expenditures, debt repayments, and dividends by 1.72x, demonstrating bulletproof financial resilience.\n\nTreasury Operations and Commercial Banking Integration:\nThe controller verifies that physical bank balances match ERP cash ledgers across all operating accounts, fixed deposit escrow accounts, and foreign currency accounts. Standard on Auditing (SA) 505 external bank confirmations are reconciled, confirming zero unrecorded disbursements or outstanding cheques exceeding statutory limits.",
        "code": "# \ud83c\udfc6 Course 01 Finale: Global Financial Controller & Master Audit Accreditation Simulator\n# Bharat Apex Global Enterprises Ltd - Master Corporate Financial Accounting Suite\n\nclass GlobalCorporateControllerMasterSuite:\n    def __init__(self, enterprise: str):\n        self.enterprise = enterprise\n\n    def run_master_consolidation(self) -> dict:\n        # Module 1: Ind AS 1 Financial Position\n        total_assets = 124000000.00\n        total_equity_liab = 124000000.00\n        pat = 14966400.00\n        tci = 16566400.00\n\n        # Module 2: Ind AS 7 Cash Flow\n        cfo = 20666400.00\n        closing_cash = 10000000.00\n\n        # Module 3: Ind AS 8 Retrospective & Prospective\n        re_adjustment = 1122480.00\n        depr_reduction = 1500000.00\n\n        # Module 4: Ind AS 10 Events\n        post_bs_adjustments = 2800000.00\n        going_concern = \"Unqualified Clean Opinion\"\n\n        return {\n            \"total_assets\": total_assets,\n            \"total_equity_liab\": total_equity_liab,\n            \"pat\": pat,\n            \"tci\": tci,\n            \"cfo\": cfo,\n            \"closing_cash\": closing_cash,\n            \"re_adjustment\": re_adjustment,\n            \"depr_reduction\": depr_reduction,\n            \"post_bs_adjustments\": post_bs_adjustments,\n            \"audit_opinion\": going_concern\n        }\n\ndef run_graduation_simulation():\n    suite = GlobalCorporateControllerMasterSuite(\"Bharat Apex Global Enterprises Ltd\")\n    res = suite.run_master_consolidation()\n\n    print(f\"Enterprise: {suite.enterprise}\")\n    print(f\"Module 1 Ind AS 1 Balance Sheet Reconciled: ${res['total_assets']:,.2f} | TCI: ${res['tci']:,.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Module 2 Ind AS 7 Operating Cash Flows (CFO): ${res['cfo']:,.2f} | Closing Cash: ${res['closing_cash']:,.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Module 3 Ind AS 8 Prior Error Equity Restatement: +${res['re_adjustment']:,.2f} | Depr Saving: ${res['depr_reduction']:,.2f}\")\n    print(f\"Module 4 Ind AS 10 Adjusting Balance Sheet Events: -${res['post_bs_adjustments']:,.2f} | Audit: {res['audit_opinion']}\")\n    print(\"GLOBAL_FINANCIAL_CONTROLLER_ACCREDITATION_PASS\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run_graduation_simulation()\n",
